config BR2_PACKAGE_DOOM_ASCII
	bool "doom-ascii"
	help
	  Text-based DOOM in your terminal!

	  doom-ascii is a source port of doomgeneric that renders the
	  game using ASCII characters, Unicode block elements, or
	  Unicode braille patterns, drawn with ANSI escape codes. It
	  has no external library dependencies (no SDL, no ncurses)
	  and has no sound.

	  You will need to separately provide a DOOM IWAD file (game
	  data), e.g. the freely redistributable doom1.wad shareware
	  IWAD, and place it where the game can find it at runtime
	  (its own directory, or a directory pointed to by the
	  DOOMWADDIR environment variable). The IWAD is not
	  distributed by this package.

	  https://github.com/wojciech-graj/doom-ascii
